# Allowlist, not a blocklist: ignore everything, then un-ignore exactly what
# Dockerfile.webserver and Dockerfile.dataservice COPY (go.mod, go.sum, cmd/,
# internal/, pkg/ - verify against those files before adding anything here).
#
# The previous blocklist approach silently shipped whatever nobody had
# thought to exclude yet into the build context - in practice that meant
# data/ (a ~740 MB local index after a dev crawl), data-smoke/, and .env (the
# Cloudflare tunnel token) all rode along on every `docker compose build`.
# None of those were ever supposed to be in the context; a blocklist just
# never caught them. An allowlist is correct by construction: a new
# top-level file or directory is excluded by default and must be deliberately
# added below before either Dockerfile can COPY it.
*

!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd/
!internal/
!pkg/

# Generated templ files - regenerated inside the webserver image build.
# Scoped to *_templ.go so hand-written helpers in that package still ship.
# Must come AFTER `!internal/` above: a re-exclusion pattern only takes
# effect below the directory-level negation it narrows, not before it.
internal/web/templates/*_templ.go

# No entry needed for a host-side `go build` binary (previously /dataservice
# and /webserver here): the leading `*` above already excludes everything at
# the repo root by default, and neither binary is produced under cmd/,
# internal/ or pkg/.
